before:
Worked example:

```javascript
function lookupQuery(id) {
  return {sql:"SELECT id, title FROM notes WHERE id = ?",params:[id]};
}
console.log(lookupQuery("7"));
```
The returned value is {"sql":"SELECT id, title FROM notes WHERE id = ?","params":["7"]}.

after:
```javascript
function lookupQuery(id) {
  return {sql:"SELECT id, title FROM notes WHERE id = ?",params:[id]};
}
console.log(lookupQuery("7"));
```
The result has fixed SQL text and a params array containing the text "7". The ID is not inserted into the SQL string.
